From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: select TX rings from queue mappings

WCN6750 selects the TCL ring using skb_get_hash() to distribute flows
across its 3 TX rings, as introduced in commit 7636c9a6e7d7 ("wifi: ath11k:
Add multi TX ring support for WCN6750"). The goal was to prevent out-of-
order packet delivery that could occur with smp_processor_id()-based
selection, where packets of the same flow could end up on different rings
depending on CPU scheduling.

Change the get_ring_selector hw_ops callback signature from
get_ring_selector(struct sk_buff *skb) to get_ring_selector(u8 ac),
removing the dependency on the skb.

Merged from:
  992-01-wifi-ath11k-use-queue-mapping-for-WCN6750-ring-selection.patch
  992-02-wifi-ath11k-remove-skb-parameter-from-get_ring_selector.patch

Based on work by:
  Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez <jtornosm@redhat.com>

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260917064825.12747-1-jtornosm@redhat.com/

Signed-off-by: Jose Ignacio Tornos Martinez <jtornosm@redhat.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -108,7 +108,7 @@ int ath11k_dp_tx(struct ath11k *ar, stru
 
 	pool_id = skb_get_queue_mapping(skb) & (ATH11K_HW_MAX_QUEUES - 1);
 
-	ring_selector = ab->hw_params.hw_ops->get_ring_selector(skb);
+	ring_selector = ab->hw_params.hw_ops->get_ring_selector(skb_get_queue_mapping(skb));
 
 tcl_ring_sel:
 	tcl_ring_retry = false;
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.c
@@ -887,28 +887,14 @@ static bool ath11k_hw_wcn6855_rx_desc_ge
 			 __le32_to_cpu(desc->u.wcn6855.msdu_start.info2));
 }
 
-static u32 ath11k_hw_ipq8074_get_tcl_ring_selector(struct sk_buff *skb)
+static u32 ath11k_hw_ipq8074_get_tcl_ring_selector(u8 ac)
 {
-	/* Let the default ring selection be based on current processor
-	 * number, where one of the 3 tcl rings are selected based on
-	 * the smp_processor_id(). In case that ring
-	 * is full/busy, we resort to other available rings.
-	 * If all rings are full, we drop the packet.
-	 *
-	 * TODO: Add throttling logic when all rings are full
-	 */
 	return smp_processor_id();
 }
 
-static u32 ath11k_hw_wcn6750_get_tcl_ring_selector(struct sk_buff *skb)
+static u32 ath11k_hw_wcn6750_get_tcl_ring_selector(u8 ac)
 {
-	/* Select the TCL ring based on the flow hash of the SKB instead
-	 * of CPU ID. Since applications pumping the traffic can be scheduled
-	 * on multiple CPUs, there is a chance that packets of the same flow
-	 * could end on different TCL rings, this could sometimes results in
-	 * an out of order arrival of the packets at the receiver.
-	 */
-	return skb_get_hash(skb);
+	return ac;
 }
 
 const struct ath11k_hw_ops ipq9574_ops = {
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/hw.h
@@ -278,7 +278,7 @@ struct ath11k_hw_ops {
 	u16 (*mpdu_info_get_peerid)(struct hal_rx_mpdu_info *mpdu_info);
 	bool (*rx_desc_mac_addr2_valid)(struct hal_rx_desc *desc);
 	u8* (*rx_desc_mpdu_start_addr2)(struct hal_rx_desc *desc);
-	u32 (*get_ring_selector)(struct sk_buff *skb);
+	u32 (*get_ring_selector)(u8 ac);
 };
 
 extern const struct ath11k_hw_ops ipq9574_ops;
